  "statement": "Expand $(1+x)^{1/2}$ in ascending powers of $x$ up to the term in $x^{3}$, and use it to estimate $\\sqrt{1.1}$.",
  "solution": "$(1+x)^{1/2}=1+\\tfrac12x+\\tfrac{(1/2)(-1/2)}{2!}x^{2}+\\tfrac{(1/2)(-1/2)(-3/2)}{3!}x^{3}+\\cdots =1+\\tfrac12x-\\tfrac18x^{2}+\\tfrac{1}{16}x^{3}+\\cdots$. For $\\sqrt{1.1}$ take $x=0.1$: $1+0.05-0.00125+0.0000625\\approx 1.0488125$.",
  "hints": [
    "Apply the generalised binomial theorem with exponent $1/2$.",
    "Substitute $x=0.1$ to estimate $\\sqrt{1.1}$."
  ],
